WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.840
Привет, Фрэнс!

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:06.740
Welcome to привет русский, Episode 57412 июля 2026 года.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.340
I'm Olya, and we've got some great Russian words to learn today.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.040
Поехали, let's go!

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.820
Our word of the day is «счастливы».

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.540
«Счастливы» – «сейт» with me slowly.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.120
«Счаст» – «ли» – «в».

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.700
Now at natural speed – «счастливы».

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:21.860
It means «Happy».

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.400
Picture your chest feeling with joy, like a chest of liveliness.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.300
Here's a simple sentence, «я счастливы»,

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.160
that means «I am happy».

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.140
Repeat after me – «счастливы» – «счастливы» – «счастливы».

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.100
Now let's build more words about feelings.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.440
Our next word is «грусность», «грусность».

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.540
It means «set», repeat after me – «грусность».

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.220
It can feel this way too, as in «кот-грусный».

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.600
That means the cat is set.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.020
Think of the sound «гр», when you feel down.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.160
Next comes «устал».

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.580
«устал» – it means tired.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.180
Repeat after me – «устал» – «устал».

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.320
You can say «я, устал» после школы.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.000
That means «I am tired after school».

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.360
Imagine you stole when you were too tired to move.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.180
Our next feeling word is «веселый».

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.940
«Веселый» – «it means cheerful or merry».

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:10.680
Repeat after me – «веселый» – «веселый» – «веселый».

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.800
Try «друг-веселый», that means my friend is cheerful.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.160
It sounds a bit like very jolly.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:18.680
Now we have «злой» – «злой».

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:19.540
It means angry.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.200
Repeat after me – «злой» – «злой».

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.340
You might hear on «злой» сегодня.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.740
That means «he is angry today».

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.940
Picture an angry toy stomping around.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:32.020
Our next word is «испуганный» – «испуганный».

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:33.300
It means «скерт».

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.300
Repeat after me – «испуганный» – «испуганный» – «испуганный».

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.540
A small animal can feel this like «мышь испуганная».

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:40.940
That means the mouse is scared.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.540
Think of getting the pool scared out of you.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.000
Here is «покойный».

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.700
«спокойный» – «it means calm».

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.140
Repeat after me – «спокойный» – «спокойный» – «спокойный».

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.920
You can say «мама-спокойный».

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.960
That means month-over-month is calm.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.400
It sounds like so quiet.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.480
Finally, try the useful phrase «я чувствую».

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.260
«Я чувствую».

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.360
It means «I feel».

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.620
Repeat after me – «я чувствую».

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.580
«Я чувствую».

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.880
You can finish it with a feeling like «я чувствую радость».

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.480
That means «I feel joy».

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.880
«Чувствую» – «you» and the word clicks right in.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.540
In Russian, words like «счастливый» – «change their ending to much the person».

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.460
For a boy or a male speaker, we keep «счастливый».

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.860
For a girl, it becomes «счастливая».

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.080
The ending tells us who feels the emotion.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.400
It works the same way with «грустный» or «усталый».

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.680
Now you can describe exactly who feels happy, said or tired.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.320
Russians ask, как «зела» to learn how someone really feels.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.840
Sharing emotions openly is part of warm family talk.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.980
Children learn orally to name their feelings, just like we did today.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.740
Draw faces for happy, said and tired.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.160
Then label each with the Russian word, or tell someone a dinner я счастливый,

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.140
or я «грустный», and say «ва» in one short sentence.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.760
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.560
Want to know a secret about «счастливый»?

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:01.180
Did you know that «счастливый» and the English word «Happy» are cousins from an ancient route?

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.080
It began as good fortune in Proto-Slavic, moved through all church Slavonic

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.800
and landed in modern Russian.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.180
The similar sounding chest has nothing to do with it,

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:14.020
because «счастливый» comes from sharing a part of luck.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:18.040
Next time you feel happy, remember it travels with «счастливый»

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.920
from the same idea of good fortune.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.280
That link is your shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.600
Молодец, that means well done.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.700
Remember, every expert started as a beginner.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:32.380
Practice saying today's words out loud, even just once,

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.600
and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.760
See you next time, «пока», that's Russian for buy.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.000
And if you'd rather watch, then listen, find us on YouTube at «нера-ар-ю».

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.160
Links in the show notes.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:47.920
Этот выпуск озвучен с помощью и и синтеза голоса.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.040
Подбор тем и анализ остаются за человеком.
